daharness (0.1.0+pkg2) kali; urgency=high

  * F1, gateway auth armable from the package: conffile gains
    GATEWAY_API_KEY (postinst generates a random key when the
    placeholder is empty) and GATEWAY_HOST (system profile pin,
    127.0.0.1); bootstrap GATEWAY_HOST/GATEWAY_PORT knobs replace the
    hardcoded 0.0.0.0:5000 (loopback default, ZAP pattern); api_gateway
    logs a boot-time error on unauthenticated + non-loopback binds.
  * F2, /etc/daharness/daharness.env is now live: EnvironmentFile= on
    the daemon + kernel units (chroma already read it); the inert
    Environment=DAHARNESS_ENV and duplicate BRAIN_SOCKET unit lines are
    dropped, so daemon/kernel/chroma all resolve WORKSPACE_ROOT through
    the StateDirectory-conffile chain.
  * F3/F4/F5: daharness-safety(7) bind + auth posture section;
    daharness.env(5) LOADING section rewritten to the implemented wiring;
    .env.example OPEN_TERMINAL residue dropped; runbook Python-3.13
    blurb refreshed to 3.14 and step-9 gateway smoke carries the API key.
  * Optional engagement-Postgres lane: /usr/bin/daharness-pg
    (init|start|stop|status) provisions a dedicated 'daharness' cluster
    on 5433 (msfdb's main cluster on 5432 untouched), creates the harness
    db + lane roles from the now-installed init bundle, and writes
    per-lane passwords to root:daharness 0640 /etc/daharness/pg.env
    (daharness-pg.1). Units gain tolerant EnvironmentFile=-pg.env; conffile
    documents HARNESS_DB_* knobs; postgresql added to Suggests. Lane is
    inert until an operator runs daharness-pg init.
  * Secretary chat lane trimmed for the headless build: bootstrap's
    interactive branch (secretary _chat + boot-time indexing) is removed,
    bare `daharness` now foregrounds the services stack exactly like
    --daemon; SECRETARY_MODEL dropped from /etc/daharness/daharness.env
    (no packaged lane reads it; EMBED_MODEL/OLLAMA_BASE_URL stay for the
    registry/memory lanes). The driving LLM headless is external
    (Open WebUI / gateway client); daharness-tools(7) rewritten.
  Follow-up: daharness-index(1) — the operator re-index wrapper (the
  runbook's discovery smoke would otherwise hit an empty registry).
  * packaging repair (VM 2026-10-20): replkit/ was missing from the
    staged tree, so daharness-repl and the kernel unit died instantly
    with "No module named replkit" (tool_repl imports it top-level);
    the tree-copy loop now stages replkit alongside the other packages.
  (evasion/ was never missing — it has been in the tree-copy set since
  pkg1; its absence would fail discovery coverage, not imports.)
  * teardown repair: _child_log_fds AttributeError killed
    daharness.service on a fresh install. stop()'s reap popped the
    child-log-fd table directly, but registration is lazy at the spawn
    sites; on a deb where ZAP's launcher is absent and MSF is not
    installed, the Brain is the only child and (until now) also
    registered nothing, so any teardown (SIGTERM or the finally after a
    launch error) died with AttributeError, masking the original error.
    The reap is now getattr-tolerant and the Brain's spawn site
    registers its /tmp/brain.log fd like the MSF/ZAP/Playwright sites
    (closes a standing fd leak too).

 -- daharness packaging <operator@localhost>  Mon, 20 Oct 2026 07:56:00 -0600

daharness (0.1.0+pkg1) kali; urgency=medium

  * First packaged build: debhelper 13 lane; frameit.so compiled at build
    time from tracked sources (unguarded module-level CDLL = build gate);
    systemd system units (no-start; operator enables), /etc conffile,
    six man pages, user-profile unit examples under /usr/share/doc.

